  "body": "Since the current definition of CustomElementConstructor made by https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/3703 looks inconstructable, that change broke TypeScript. The following code is invalid now on TypeScript@3.8.0-dev.20200101.\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nwindow.customElements.define('custom-tag', class extends HTMLElement { });\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\nArgument of type 'typeof (Anonymous class)' is not assignable to parameter of type 'CustomElementConstructor'.\r\nType 'typeof (Anonymous class)' provides no match for the signature '(): HTMLElement'.ts(2345)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIs the current definition of CustomElementConstructor is wrong? Or `callback CustomElementConstructor = HTMLElement ();` should be read as constructable?",
